                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "b88ce182-e0c0-303c-b8cb-e99ad0ac66fb",
                        "entry_id": "73917b01-f3ab-3625-b4b9-80f1367af17f",
                        "glosses": [
                            "zwyczajowe prawo małżeńskie nakazujące poślubienie wdowy przez brata lub nawet przez spadkobiercę jej zmarłego męża (nawet jeśli jest żonaty), w celu zapewnienia ciągłości rodu, obowiązujące u ludów Azji (Arabów, Hindusów, Mongołów) oraz plemion afrykańskich"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "38c9eb58-5663-4963-8e7f-41b64d463e05",
                                "sense_id": "b88ce182-e0c0-303c-b8cb-e99ad0ac66fb",
                                "text": "Potomek męski mężczyzny, który poddał się prawu lewiratu, jest traktowany jako syn zmarłego brata."
                            }
                        ],
                        "sense_index_json": "\"1.1\""
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "4322e998-9f0c-4dc3-b826-161d7e049fe2",
                        "source_entry_id": "73917b01-f3ab-3625-b4b9-80f1367af17f",
                        "source_sense_id": "b88ce182-e0c0-303c-b8cb-e99ad0ac66fb",
                        "target_lang_word": "levirate",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "levirate",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "6c9bfe06-633a-39a2-8cc1-8363f72e3f10",
                                        "entry_id": "064fd201-5216-3fd4-9def-714d46c9511f",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Having to do with one's husband's brother."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "not-comparable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "levirate",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "ac80d206-3fdd-3da0-941e-9afd7c779d75",
                                        "entry_id": "9302079b-8d62-304a-a7a5-babc4302a4dc",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A marriage between a widow and her deceased husband's brother or, sometimes, heir."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "ff0d17f8-fce8-3dde-8480-d5102fbbf41f",
                                        "entry_id": "9302079b-8d62-304a-a7a5-babc4302a4dc",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "The institution of levirate marriage."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "d02bc252-9a2e-420c-834a-e71dee22a6b6",
                                                "sense_id": "ff0d17f8-fce8-3dde-8480-d5102fbbf41f",
                                                "text": "And it is, he says, impossible not to believe that the Levirate—that is, the practice of marrying a dead brother's widow—is derived from polyandry."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "58ac0e34-af86-4aec-a9f0-268e167adb70",
                                                "sense_id": "ff0d17f8-fce8-3dde-8480-d5102fbbf41f",
                                                "text": "It is only a secondary purpose of the levirate that the property of the deceased passes on to the one who is heir to his name, and is probably a later accretion."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "5d0610b6-a18c-49df-ab80-84802bf81f47",
                                                "sense_id": "ff0d17f8-fce8-3dde-8480-d5102fbbf41f",
                                                "text": "The levirate is found in patrilineal societies in which the bride marries into her husband's family while essentially severing her ties with her original family."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
